        <string>Beautiful omega with fixed two-part ornament</string>
        <key>nativeBodyConstruction</key>
        <dict>
          <key>caseSpecificBowlSource</key>
          <string>uni0441.sc</string>
          <key>construction</key>
          <string>Use two genuine same-cut, same-case Cyrillic Es bowls facing inward, preserving all bowl curves, stroke weights and terminal cuts. Join their lower terminals with a native-omega-weight rising middle stroke. Reflection is performed in the native italic axis and returned to that same axis; no upright is used as a synthetic italic. This open-top broad omega differs from the existing W-like Cyrillic omega. No source glyph is scaled.</string>
          <key>kind</key>
          <string>Native broad omega with inward bowls and rising middle stroke</string>
